## Independent practice

Complete each item. Use complete sentences and text evidence where asked.

1. Practice 1: On a short fiction scene at dusk, mark (1) a claim-bearing sentence, (2) one charged word, (3) one structural move. Write a 2-sentence warrant linking mark #2 to meaning.
2. Practice 2: On a drama scene with stage directions, mark (1) a claim-bearing sentence, (2) one charged word, (3) one structural move. Write a 2-sentence warrant linking mark #2 to meaning.
3. Practice 3: On an editorial on local civic life, mark (1) a claim-bearing sentence, (2) one charged word, (3) one structural move. Write a 2-sentence warrant linking mark #2 to meaning.
4. Practice 4: On a public-domain speech excerpt, mark (1) a claim-bearing sentence, (2) one charged word, (3) one structural move. Write a 2-sentence warrant linking mark #2 to meaning.
5. Practice 5: On a paired set of letters on the same event, mark (1) a claim-bearing sentence, (2) one charged word, (3) one structural move. Write a 2-sentence warrant linking mark #2 to meaning.
6. Practice 6: On a poem about a river crossing, mark (1) a claim-bearing sentence, (2) one charged word, (3) one structural move. Write a 2-sentence warrant linking mark #2 to meaning.

### Answer key (quality bar)

*These keys describe strong responses — exact wording will vary.*

1. Strong work names exact text, explains the charged word''s effect, and connects structure to the narrator''s certainty is incomplete.
2. Strong work names exact text, explains the charged word''s effect, and connects structure to silence carries meaning.
3. Strong work names exact text, explains the charged word''s effect, and connects structure to evidence must outweigh slogans.
4. Strong work names exact text, explains the charged word''s effect, and connects structure to duty requires courage under pressure.
5. Strong work names exact text, explains the charged word''s effect, and connects structure to perspective reshapes fact selection.
6. Strong work names exact text, explains the charged word''s effect, and connects structure to movement signals a moral choice.

## Exit ticket

1. One-sentence definition of today''s skill in your own words.
2. One mistake you will refuse to make on the next timed task.
3. One text evidence habit you will keep from this lesson.

## Wrap-up

College-ready ELA is **claim + evidence + warrant**, revised. Next lesson continues Unit 1: Close Reading & Annotation.
