4. Practice 4: Using a poem about a river crossing, write a short analytical paragraph (6–8 sentences) that advances a claim related to “Choosing a Throughline” with one embedded quotation and a warrant.
5. Practice 5: Using a short fiction scene at dusk, write a short analytical paragraph (6–8 sentences) that advances a claim related to “Choosing a Throughline” with one embedded quotation and a warrant.
6. Practice 6: Using a drama scene with stage directions, write a short analytical paragraph (6–8 sentences) that advances a claim related to “Choosing a Throughline” with one embedded quotation and a warrant.

